cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying preprint, please cite it as below."
title: "Hyphae v2: Hash-Chained Verbatim Quotation — A Verifiable Provenance Layer for Grounded Retrieval"
abstract: >-
  Hyphae is a verifiable-provenance layer for grounded retrieval: it answers by
  emitting byte-identical quotations of stored memory fragments over a SHA-256
  hash-chained journal, with no large language model in the cognition path, so
  every output span can be independently audited back to named, unaltered
  source fragments. The accompanying preprint frames verifiable provenance as an
  addable, realizer-independent layer, uses a trivial echo (and echo+journal)
  control to show that measured correctness and grounding are properties of
  verbatim quotation rather than of the system, and argues that citation
  faithfulness is made trivially true by construction. Version 2 implements and
  adversarially demonstrates the full provenance stack -- external head anchor,
  append-only ledger (freshness and non-equivocation), external witness (entry
  withholding), signed keyring (key rotation), and a C2PA-aligned ingestion
  bridge -- with a community-scale provenance benchmark and a multi-hop harness,
  evaluated against 18 LLM-based configurations across two corpora.
